subject: test(kilo): regression test for free-models fetch timeout guard (GAP-P3-26)

The AbortSignal.timeout(10000) on the Kilo models fetch already exists at
HEAD (present since the original commit 8640503b, 2026-03-31) — the gap
scanner flagged a false positive at route.js:19.

This regression test locks the behavior so the guard cannot be silently
removed:

- route.js contains signal: AbortSignal.timeout() on the Kilo fetch
- timeout is exactly 10 000 ms
- signal is on the same fetch() call that uses KILO_MODELS_URL

Anti-false-positive verified: intentionally removing the signal line from
route.js makes all 3 assertions fail; git-checkout restore returns to 3/3
pass.

